00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
am i a person a voice or a raccoon  what am i marvel sure has some unique  techniques they used when casting the  eternals and for some of them securing  their roles proved to be quite easy  being mexican a woman and my age it felt  like they were punking me  for the longest time angelina jolie was  one of the biggest stars who had yet to  join a superhero movie previous to  eternals the oscar winner actress had  even turned down another high-profile  superhero role jolie really gravitated  to eternals because of its  character-driven nature funnily enough  initially jolie wasn't even told what  character she would be playing in the  film which led jolie to ponder just how  big or small her role was going to be  jolie's kids had some important  questions for her when she revealed to  them she was joining the franchise i  think the first question was what color  are you  when jolie assured her kids that she'd  still look somewhat like herself on  screen they quickly asked what her  powers would be jolie noted that her  kids were very quick to get a hint of  who her character was despite none of  the characters in eternals being  household names  when marvel initially approached salma  hayek about joining the marvel cinematic  universe she was ready to turn them down  hayek had been a bit frustrated about  never being approached to play a  superhero he didn't come in my 20s he  didn't come in my 30s and come in my 40s  and all of the sudden they show up in my  50s hayek initially assumed that the  studio wanted her to play a grandmother  sort of role thinking that her role was  some kind of extra or an old prostitute  once she learned the director was chloe  zhao hayek had a change of heart and met  with marvel in the comics hayek's  character ajax is traditionally played  as a man but the role was gender swapped  for the big screen hayek claimed that  this decision was a beautiful shocker to  her hayek admits that she was a bit  intimidated at first as despite being  told that she'd have a major role in the  movie she wasn't given a script had to  enter negotiations and sign a contract  and wasn't able to tell anybody about  the exciting new turn in her career  kit harrington made waves as jon snow on  game of thrones and marvel head honcho  kevin feige had been eyeing harrington  for quite some time a year before  harrington was cast as dane whitman  harrington had actually had a general  meeting with phage about potentially  joining the franchise a year passed by  and harrington received a call from the  film's producer nate moore about joining  the eternals as dane whitman who in the  comics goes on to become the superhero  black knight they'd said look it's not a  major part size-wise in this movie but  it's a really interesting character that  could go somewhere cool i did some  reading up on it and then i said yes  just like his days as jon snow on game  of thrones harrington had to be quite  secretive on who exactly he would be  playing in the eternals but of course he  was prepared i think if there was a  school for that then  game of thrones is a pretty good school  to go through leah mchugh is one of the  more unknown names out of the ensemble  cast of eternals that being said miku's  addition to play sprite wasn't her first  experience with the marvel universe when  she was younger the 14 year old actress  had auditioned for roles in several  marvel television shows though this time  it was a bit different while she was  auditioning in the same location as  before she wasn't told if the project  was related to marvel all the  description read for the character was  for a character with dark eyes and dark  hair which led to mchugh telling the  casting team that she was willing to dye  her hair and wear contacts i think my  second round of callbacks i finally got  real sides and i was sort of able to  figure out who sprite was by googling  and i was like oh my gosh this is for an  eternal i could play a superhero the  next call from marvel was the ultimate  dream come true for mchugh when i first  got the call i was like overwhelmed with  emotions  kumail nanjiani is not typically an  actor you'd expect to play a superhero  but given all the funny men boarding  superhero films it shouldn't be too much  of a shocker when marvel had approached  nanjiani about playing a superhero in  the eternals movie nanjiani proved that  he didn't need much swaying to board the  project  yes i literally said yes  right in the room in fact the only  person nanjiani initially told about the  role was his wife when it came down to  working on how he would play kingo he  had a pretty blunt discussion with  director chloe zhao i was like okay so  how do you see kingo she was like he's  you i picked you because i wanted him to  be you nanjiani ended up going through  quite the transformation for the role in  terms of his body despite the director's  wishes to have him keep his regular body  type  lauren ridloff's breakout role in the  hit television series the walking dead  helped get marvel's attention ridloff  didn't exactly have to audition for the  role rather she was tapped by chloe zhao  and producer nate moore the director  asked her about her passions in life to  which she responded reading running and  the arts from there the conversation  shifted to the eternals and finally to  the character of makari who in the  comics is typically portrayed as male  ridloff was previously unfamiliar with  the character but did her research after  that fateful meeting and the next time  she met with the director and producer  they offered her the role  brian tyree henry was quite emotional  when marvel approached him to play  fastos in eternals describing it as an  out of body experience henry said he was  at a loss for words when he was cast and  that the feeling he felt upon learning  the news is a difficult sensation to  explain you just say yes and you cry and  then you can't tell anybody anything so  then you cry some more  kevin feige has said that the true lead  of the film is gemma chan who plays  cersei oddly enough despite being the  main character the actress was one of  the last people cast for the film  producer nate moore revealed that she  wasn't even the first choice for the  role since she had already had a role in  the mcu movie captain marvel as the  blue-skinned minerva after bringing in  chan for a line reading the casting team  realized that she truly was perfect for  the part and that her inclusion wouldn't  be nearly as distracting as minerva and  cersei are two characters that look  completely different from one another  chan claims that she was pleasantly  surprised when she was offered the lead  role i was as surprised as anyone else i  i was not expecting to be back chan was  already close friends with richard  madden prior to being cast in the role  of cersei but the thought of getting to  work with her longtime friend made her  even more excited to join the cast i  obviously jumped at the chance and to  get to work with richard madden and the  rest of the amazing cast it's great  barry kyon had long been a fan of marvel  superheroes and had even made a tweet  back in 2013 hoping to one day become a  superhero on screen it was a dream come  true when he was approached to play drug  in eternals i would say it's a pinch me  moment and i would say i still won't  realize that until it comes out probably  you know it's going to be a nice feeling  then  according to don lee he was the creative  team's first and only choice when it  came down to the character gilgamesh lee  is already a hugely successful actor in  korea starring in blockbusters such as  train to busan the outlaws and the  neighbors after the international  success of train to busan these fames  started to go even beyond korea i  received numerous offers from hollywood  i got a call from the casting director  of eternals who offered me the role of  gilgamesh chloe zhao and nate moore had  in fact already seen many of lee's films  and analyzed his character even before  lee said yes to the role it definitely  seems like that even if lee told marvel  no they would not have taken it as an  answer thankfully lee happily obliged  for his first major role in an american  production  chloe zhao didn't set out to build  another a-list marvel cast for the  eternals and instead intended to look  for actors who could bring themselves to  the roles yet in the end the eternals  cast may just be one of the most  impressive groups of actors in the  entire mcu  what has been your favorite cast in a  marvel movie

